<title>GERMANY: Adtranz buys majority of Polish Pafawag.</title>
<headline>Adtranz buys majority of Polish Pafawag.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>European railway group Adtranz said on Tuesday it had taken a 75 percent stake in the Polish railway infrastructure-producer Pafawag for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Adtranz, a 50-50 joint venture between Germany's Daimler-Benz AG and Swiss-Swedish engineering firm ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG, said some 45 million marks ($26.4 million) was due to be invested in the Polish firm's plant in Wroclaw. Pafawag employs some 1,600 workers.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.707 German Marks)</p>
